course: dictionary
lesson: 7342
title: Words for things we make
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Plasticine is a noun, a naming word for a thing. It is a soft, coloured modelling material, a bit like clay, that never dries out. You can press it, roll it and reshape it again and again, which is why children use it to make animals, letters and shapes.
explain: Read the words around a word to find its meaning. «Cold muscles are like cold plasticine: stiff and quick to tear.» Stiff and quick to tear tell you that plasticine is firm when cold and can rip easily. A comparison like this helps you picture a word.
explain: Plasticine is uncountable, so you say some plasticine or a lump of plasticine, not a plasticine. Phrases like «a lump/ball of plasticine» and «plasticine model» show how it is used. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: a soft, coloured modelling material still makes sense.
fact: Plasticine is a noun, a naming word.
fact: Plasticine is a soft, coloured modelling material, like clay, that never dries out.
fact: Uncountable nouns have no plural: say some plasticine, not two plasticines.
fact: In science, a plasticine boat can float while the same lump, shaped as a ball, sinks.
fact: «Stop-motion» means moving models a tiny bit, taking a photo and repeating; «Wallace and Gromit» are made this way with plasticine by the British studio Aardman.
exercise: «Cold muscles are like cold plasticine: stiff and quick to tear.» What does stiff suggest about cold plasticine? | Soft and runny | Warm and bouncy | *Firm and hard to bend | Bright and shiny
exercise: In science, the same lump of plasticine sinks as a ball but floats as a boat shape. What is this test about? | Cooking dinner | Singing songs | Counting numbers | *Floating and sinking
exercise: Ella says plasticine is a kind of cake. What is plasticine really? | A sweet, sticky cake | A type of petrol for cars | A kind of paper for drawing | *A soft, coloured modelling material like clay
test: «Stop-motion means moving models a tiny bit, taking a photo and repeating.» Which models are made this way with plasticine? | Wooden chairs | Paper aeroplanes | *Wallace and Gromit | Clocks and watches
test: What word class is plasticine in a sentence? | *Noun | Adverb | Verb | Adjective
exam: Which is correct for talking about plasticine in general? | two plasticines | *some plasticine | a plasticine | many plasticine lumps of plasticines
